{"id":"mahabharata-13-078","work":"mahabharata","part":13,"partName":"अनुशासनपर्व","partNameEn":"Anushasana Parva","unit":78,"title":"अष्टसप्ततितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 78 · Gifts of cows and the worlds they win","summary":{"en":"Vasishtha says that the cows were made by Brahma after a long austerity so as to rise to the highest state, and lists the worlds won by one who gives a cow with her calf, such as the moon's world for a spotted cow. He says that for as many years as the cow has hairs, the giver is honoured in heaven and is then born in a good family on earth.","kn":"ಬ್ರಹ್ಮ ದೀರ್ಘ ತಪಸ್ಸಿನ ನಂತರ ಉನ್ನತ ಸ್ಥಿತಿ ಪಡೆಯಲು ಗೋವುಗಳನ್ನು ಸೃಷ್ಟಿಸಿದನೆಂದು ವಸಿಷ್ಠ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಕರುವಿನೊಡನೆ ಹಸು ಕೊಟ್ಟವನು ಪಡೆಯುವ ಲೋಕಗಳ ಪಟ್ಟಿ. ಹಸುವಿನ ರೋಮಗಳಷ್ಟು ವರ್ಷ ಸ್ವರ್ಗದಲ್ಲಿ ಗೌರವ ಪಡೆದು ನಂತರ ಭೂಮಿಯಲ್ಲಿ ಒಳ್ಳೆಯ ಕುಲದಲ್ಲಿ ಹುಟ್ಟುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"वसिष्ठ कहते हैं कि ब्रह्मा ने दीर्घ तप के बाद गौओं को उच्च पद पाने के लिए बनाया, और बछड़े सहित गौ देने वाले को मिलने वाले लोक गिनाते हैं, जैसे चितकबरी गाय के लिए चन्द्रलोक। वे कहते हैं कि गाय के जितने रोम हैं उतने वर्ष दाता स्वर्ग में सम्मानित होता है और फिर पृथ्वी पर अच्छे कुल में जन्मता है।","te":"బ్రహ్మ దీర్ఘ తపస్సు తరువాత ఉన్నత స్థితి పొందేందుకు ఆవులను సృష్టించాడని వసిష్ఠుడు చెబుతాడు; దూడతో ఆవునిచ్చేవాడు పొందే లోకాల పట్టిక ఇస్తాడు. ఆవుకు ఉన్న రోమాల సంఖ్య ఏళ్లు స్వర్గంలో గౌరవం పొంది, తరువాత భూమిపై మంచి కులంలో పుడతాడని అంటాడు.","ta":"பிரம்மன் நீண்ட தவத்துக்குப் பின் உயர்நிலை அடைவதற்காகப் பசுக்களைப் படைத்தான் என்று வசிஷ்டர் கூறி, கன்றுடன் பசு தருபவன் பெறும் உலகங்களைப் பட்டியலிடுகிறார். பசுவின் மயிர்கள் அளவு ஆண்டுகள் சொர்க்கத்தில் மதிக்கப்பட்டுப் பின் பூமியில் நல்ல குலத்தில் பிறப்பான் என்கிறார்.","ml":"പശുക്കളെ ഉത്തമമായ അവസ്ഥയിലേക്ക് ഉയരാൻ ബ്രഹ്മാവ് ദീർഘ തപസ്സിനുശേഷം സൃഷ്ടിച്ചതാണെന്ന് വസിഷ്ഠൻ പറയുന്നു; കിടാവിനോടൊപ്പം പശുവിനെ ദാനം ചെയ്യുന്നവൻ നേടുന്ന ലോകങ്ങൾ അദ്ദേഹം പട്ടികപ്പെടുത്തുന്നു; പുള്ളിപ്പശുവിനെ ദാനം ചെയ്യുന്നവന് ചന്ദ്രലോകം ലഭിക്കുന്നതുപോലെ. പശുവിന്റെ ദേഹത്തുള്ള രോമങ്ങളുടെ എണ്ണത്തോളം വർഷം ദാതാവ് സ്വർഗ്ഗത്തിൽ ആദരിക്കപ്പെടുമെന്നും, പിന്നീട് ഭൂമിയിൽ നല്ല കുലത്തിൽ ജനിക്കുമെന്നും അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 13.78; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Nov 03 2026","sections":[{"title":"आनुशासनिकपर्व","titleEn":"Anushasanika Parva (The instructions)","verses":[{"text":"वसिष्ठ उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vasishtha said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"शतं वर्षसहस्राणां तपस्तप्तं सुदुश्चरम् ।\nगोभिः पूर्वविसृष्टाभिर्गच्छेम श्रेष्ठतामिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The cows, who were created earlier, practised a very hard austerity for a hundred thousand years, thinking, 'May we reach excellence.'"}},{"n":2,"text":"लोकेऽस्मिन्दक्षिणानां च सर्वासां वयमुत्तमाः ।\nभवेम न च लिप्येम दोषेणेति परंतप ॥","meaning":{"en":"'O scorcher of foes, may we be the best of all gifts in this world, and may no fault stain us.'"}},{"n":3,"text":"स एव चेतसा तेन हतो लिप्येत सर्वदा ।\nशकृता च पवित्रार्थं कुर्वीरन्देवमानुषाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"'One who is struck down by that very thought would always be stained; and gods and men should use our dung for purification.'"}},{"n":4,"text":"तथा सर्वाणि भूतानि स्थावराणि चराणि च ।\nप्रदातारश्च गोलोकान्गच्छेयुरिति मानद ॥","meaning":{"en":"'And may all beings, moving and unmoving, and the givers of cows, O giver of honour, go to the world of cows.'"}},{"n":5,"text":"ताभ्यो वरं ददौ ब्रह्मा तपसोऽन्ते स्वयं प्रभुः ।\nएवं भवत्विति विभुर्लोकांस्तारयतेति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the end of their austerity the lord Brahma himself gave them a boon: 'So be it; and may you carry the worlds across.'"}},{"n":6,"text":"उत्तस्थुः सिद्धिकामास्ता भूतभव्यस्य मातरः ।\nतपसोऽन्ते महाराज गावो लोकपरायणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the end of the austerity, O great king, those mothers of what was and will be, the cows, who are the refuge of the worlds, rose up, desiring success."}},{"n":7,"text":"तस्माद्गावो महाभागाः पवित्रं परमुच्यते ।\nतथैव सर्वभूतानां गावस्तिष्ठन्ति मूर्धनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore the greatly blessed cows are called supremely pure, and the cows stand on the heads of all beings."}},{"n":8,"text":"समानवत्सां कपिलां धेनुं दत्त्वा पयस्विनीम् ।\nसुव्रतां वस्त्रसंवीतां ब्रह्मलोके महीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who gives a tawny milch cow with a calf of equal colour, well-behaved and covered in cloth, is honoured in Brahma's world."}},{"n":9,"text":"रोहिणीं तुल्यवत्सां तु धेनुं दत्त्वा पयस्विनीम् ।\nसुव्रतां वस्त्रसंवीतां सूर्यलोके महीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who gives a Rohini cow giving milk with a calf like her, well-behaved and covered in cloth, is honoured in the sun's world."}},{"n":10,"text":"समानवत्सां शबलां धेनुं दत्त्वा पयस्विनीम् ।\nसुव्रतां वस्त्रसंवीतां सोमलोके महीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who gives a dappled milch cow with a matching calf, well-behaved and covered in cloth, is honoured in the moon's world."}},{"n":11,"text":"समानवत्सां श्वेतां तु धेनुं दत्त्वा पयस्विनीम् ।\nसुव्रतां वस्त्रसंवीतामिन्द्रलोके महीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who gives a white milch cow with a matching calf, well-behaved and covered in cloth, is honoured in Indra's world."}},{"n":12,"text":"समानवत्सां कृष्णां तु धेनुं दत्त्वा पयस्विनीम् ।\nसुव्रतां वस्त्रसंवीतामग्निलोके महीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who gives a black milch cow with a matching calf, well-behaved and covered in cloth, is honoured in the world of Agni."}},{"n":13,"text":"समानवत्सां धूम्रां तु धेनुं दत्त्वा पयस्विनीम् ।\nसुव्रतां वस्त्रसंवीतां याम्यलोके महीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who gives a smoke-grey milch cow with a matching calf, well-behaved and covered in cloth, is honoured in the world of Yama."}},{"n":14,"text":"अपां फेनसवर्णां तु सवत्सां कांस्यदोहनाम् ।\nप्रदाय वस्त्रसंवीतां वारुणं लोकमश्नुते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who gives a cow the colour of water-foam, with her calf and a bronze milk pail, covered in cloth, reaches the world of Varuna."}},{"n":15,"text":"वातरेणुसवर्णां तु सवत्सां कांस्यदोहनाम् ।\nप्रदाय वस्त्रसंवीतां वायुलोके महीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who gives a cow the colour of wind-blown dust, with her calf and a bronze milk pail, covered in cloth, is honoured in the world of Vayu."}},{"n":16,"text":"हिरण्यवर्णां पिङ्गाक्षीं सवत्सां कांस्यदोहनाम् ।\nप्रदाय वस्त्रसंवीतां कौबेरं लोकमश्नुते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who gives a golden cow with tawny eyes, with her calf and a bronze milk pail, covered in cloth, reaches the world of Kubera."}},{"n":17,"text":"पलालधूम्रवर्णां तु सवत्सां कांस्यदोहनाम् ।\nप्रदाय वस्त्रसंवीतां पितृलोके महीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who gives a cow the colour of straw-smoke, with her calf and a bronze milk pail, covered in cloth, is honoured in the world of the ancestors."}},{"n":18,"text":"सवत्सां पीवरीं दत्त्वा शितिकण्ठामलंकृताम् ।\nवैश्वदेवमसंबाधं स्थानं श्रेष्ठं प्रपद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who gives a plump cow with her calf and a dark neck, adorned, reaches the excellent unobstructed place of the Vishvadevas."}},{"n":19,"text":"समानवत्सां गौरीं तु धेनुं दत्त्वा पयस्विनीम् ।\nसुव्रतां वस्त्रसंवीतां वसूनां लोकमश्नुते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who gives a fair milch cow with a matching calf, well-behaved and covered in cloth, reaches the world of the Vasus."}},{"n":20,"text":"पाण्डुकम्बलवर्णां तु सवत्सां कांस्यदोहनाम् ।\nप्रदाय वस्त्रसंवीतां साध्यानां लोकमश्नुते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who gives a cow the colour of a pale blanket, with her calf and a bronze milk pail, covered in cloth, reaches the world of the Sadhyas."}},{"n":21,"text":"वैराटपृष्ठमुक्षाणं सर्वरत्नैरलंकृतम् ।\nप्रदाय मरुतां लोकानजरान्प्रतिपद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who gives a bull with a back like a Virata, adorned with all kinds of jewels, gains the ageless worlds of the Maruts."}},{"n":22,"text":"वत्सोपपन्नां नीलाङ्गां सर्वरत्नसमन्विताम् ।\nगन्धर्वाप्सरसां लोकान्दत्त्वा प्राप्नोति मानवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who gives a dark-bodied cow with her calf and all kinds of jewels gains the worlds of the Gandharvas and Apsarases."}},{"n":23,"text":"शितिकण्ठमनड्वाहं सर्वरत्नैरलंकृतम् ।\nदत्त्वा प्रजापतेर्लोकान्विशोकः प्रतिपद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who gives a dark-necked ox adorned with all jewels reaches the worlds of Prajapati, free from sorrow."}},{"n":24,"text":"गोप्रदानरतो याति भित्त्वा जलदसंचयान् ।\nविमानेनार्कवर्णेन दिवि राजन्विराजता ॥","meaning":{"en":"One devoted to giving cows goes, O king, breaking through the masses of clouds, in a heavenly chariot shining like the sun."}},{"n":25,"text":"तं चारुवेषाः सुश्रोण्यः सहस्रं वरयोषितः ।\nरमयन्ति नरश्रेष्ठ गोप्रदानरतं नरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"O best of men, a thousand fine women of beautiful form and lovely hips delight that man devoted to giving cows."}},{"n":26,"text":"वीणानां वल्लकीनां च नूपुराणां च शिञ्जितैः ।\nहासैश्च हरिणाक्षीणां प्रसुप्तः प्रतिबोध्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he sleeps he is woken by the sound of lutes, veenas and anklets, and by the laughter of the deer-eyed women."}},{"n":27,"text":"यावन्ति लोमानि भवन्ति धेन्वा-\nस्तावन्ति वर्षाणि महीयते सः ।\nस्वर्गाच्च्युतश्चापि ततो नृलोके\nकुले समुत्पत्स्यति गोमिनां सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For as many years as there are hairs on the cow, he is honoured; and when he falls from heaven, he will be born in the world of men in a family that owns cows."}}]}]}